                <pb facs="0562" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/6302: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-10-29T12:00:00+02:00">October 29,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received October 29—7:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1033. The outbreak of hostilities with Greece has not yet been announced to the
                    Italian people either in the press or on the radio. This morning’s press however
                    carries the text of the Italian ultimatum and editorials declare that any
                    resistance on the part of Greece will be overcome by the Italian Armed
                    Forces.</p>
                <p>Text of the note will be forwarded by mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
